        "original_id": "49e13859-ae43-54c0-93c4-f1d3eb6f673b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luis Gianneo, Ariel Ramírez, Marta Lambertini, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, Rodolfo Arizaga, Roberto Caamaño, Gerardo Gandini\n- Roles: composer, pianist, conductor, music educator, music director\n- Organizations: Universidad Católica Argentina\n- Places: Argentina, San Isidro, Buenos Aires\n- Topics: Argentine folk music, music education\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Gianneo (1897–1968) was an Argentine composer, pianist, conductor, and music educator.\n- Luis Gianneo taught composers Ariel Ramírez, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, and Rodolfo Arizaga.\n- Ariel Ramírez (4 September 1921 – 18 February 2010) was an Argentine composer, pianist, and music director.\n- Ariel Ramírez was considered a chief exponent of Argentine folk music and was noted for iconic musical compositions.\n- Marta Lambertini was born in San Isidro, Buenos Aires.\n- Marta Lambertini studied at the Universidad Católica Argentina with Roberto Caamaño, Luis Gianneo, and Gerardo Gandini, and she graduated in 1972.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
